---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, withBase } from '../consts';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Contact"
  description="How to reach Fader Report: corrections, pricing updates, licensing changes and general enquiries."
>
  <h1 class="pagetitle">Contact</h1>
  <p class="lede">One address, read by a human.</p>

  <p style="font-size:1.2rem"><a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a></p>

  <h2>Especially worth emailing about</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>A price we got wrong, or that has changed.</strong> Include the page and what
      you see now. This is the single most useful thing you can send us.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Licence terms that have been updated.</strong> Vendors rewrite these quietly.
    </li>
    <li><strong>A broken link, or a page that reads like it was written by a machine that did not care.</strong></li>
    <li>
      <strong>A vendor correction.</strong> If you work for a company we cover and we have
      misread your terms, tell us and we will fix it. We will not take your marketing copy in
      exchange, and coverage is not for sale.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we will not do</h2>
  <p>
    We do not accept guest posts, paid links, sponsored reviews or link exchanges, so there is
    no need to send that email. We also cannot give legal advice on whether your specific
    release is in the clear — see the note on any licensing article for why.
  </p>

  <p>
    Our <a href={withBase('/privacy/')}>privacy policy</a> covers what happens to an email you
    send us: it is read, replied to, and not added to any list, because there is no list.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
